{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}\pard\plain \nowidctlpar\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\b\f11\cgrid0 Ever wish you could use standard data aware controls with or without the Borland Database Engine?
\par 
\par Ever wish you could display data from multiple file formats, from multiple database engines, and bypass the Borland Database Engine entirely?}{\f11\cgrid0 
\par 
\par Well, TMemData may be your solution...It does all of this, and best of all, TMemData only adds a couple dozen KB to your exe!
\par 
\par Since it only works with Memory, TMemData allows you to work with small amounts of data with lightening fast speeds.
\par 
\par TMemData supports:
\par 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-200\li200\nowidctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnindent200 {\pntxtb \'b7}}\ls1\adjustright {\f11\cgrid0 Calculated  and lookup fields
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}Sorting by any field, including calculated and lookup fields
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}Bookmarks (multiple select for grid controls)
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}Locate method
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\adjustright {\f11\cgrid0 
\par }{\b\f11\cgrid0 This powerful non-visual component allows you to save/restore data to text files, to the registry, binary format and anything else you wish to think up.}{\f11\cgrid0 
\par 
\par This Demo contains two examples using TMemData.  In both instances, data is retrieved from binary files (contacts.dat and produc
ts.dat). The first demo uses standard Delphi data controls (DBGrid,BEdit, DBLookupCombo, DBCheckBox and DBComboBox) and the second example uses the ExpressGrid by Developer Express Inc.
\par }}